  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 414 AM MDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nHeat risk is at its peak today with HEAT ADVISORIES in effect for \nmuch of Southeast Idaho from Noon today through 8 PM MDT this \nevening for temperatures near or up to 100 degrees. Temperatures \nwill gradually cool through mid-week back to around normal to \nslightly below normal. \n\nSouthwest flow will lift monsoonal moisture into Southeast Idaho \nbeginning this evening and will support daily shower and \nthunderstorm chances through mid to late week. Isolated storms will \ntrend more scattered heading later into the week with locally heavy \nrainfall and outflow winds of 40 to 50 mph. High resolution models \nshow activity primarily concentrated across central and south-\ncentral Idaho during the evening with development further east \nduring the late night and overnight hours.",
